<!--
  Status-bar notification icon.

  PLACEHOLDER — replace with the SmartEco mark. Generate the replacement with
  Android Studio: right-click res → New → Image Asset → Icon Type
  "Notification Icons", which produces the correct shape from the existing
  launcher artwork.

  The constraints are non-negotiable, whatever artwork replaces this:

    * White only, on a transparent background. Android 5+ (API 21) takes the
      ALPHA CHANNEL of this drawable and discards every colour, then tints the
      result with @color/notification_color. A full-colour icon therefore
      renders as a solid white square — the single most common visible defect
      in an FCM integration, and it shows up in the very first test.
    * Flat silhouette, no gradients, no strokes that rely on colour contrast.
    * 24dp viewport with the glyph inset from the edges; the system crops
      tightly.

  Referenced by the default_notification_icon meta-data in AndroidManifest.xml
  and by smallIcon in src/services/pushNotifications.js.
-->
